# Card & Section Header

<h2 id="purpose">Purpose</h2>

A heading names a card or a group of cards so people know what they are about to read or use. In Home Assistant the card made for this is the Heading card.

This page owns the section row, and points to [Heading](heading.html) for the Heading card. The page header of this site is a different component: see [Header](header.html). For card headings and heading levels see [Card (Base Surface)](cards.html).

This page covers:

- Card & Section Header
  - `hui-section-row`

<h2 id="anatomy">Anatomy</h2>

A section row is a divider with an optional label, inside an Entities card. For the parts, keys, styles, levels and theme settings of the Heading card, see [Heading](heading.html).

<h2 id="variants">Variants, variables and extensibility</h2>

<h3 id="child-hui-section-row"><code>hui-section-row</code></h3>

The section row (YAML `type: section`) is a divider with a label inside an Entities card. For a heading at the top of a section of a Sections view, use the Heading card (`hui-heading-card`, YAML `type: heading`). See [Heading](heading.html) for its keys, styles and limits.

The sections of a Sections view (`hui-section`, `hui-grid-section`) are layout containers and have no header of their own.

```yaml
type: entities
entities:
  - type: section
    label: Lights
  - light.kitchen
```

A section row is a divider and an optional label. It is a plain block, not a heading, so it does not appear in a heading list for assistive technology.

The section row’s label uses `primary-text-color`, or `section-header-text-color` if you set it. The theme sets nothing for the section row colours. Changing them needs card-mod, if they can be changed at all. Theme settings for the Heading card are on [Heading](heading.html).

<h2 id="limits">Advantages and limitations</h2>

- The Heading card is native, so it works with every Sections view. Its limits are on [Heading](heading.html).
- The section row is only a divider and label, so use it for visual grouping, not for navigation.
- A section row is not a heading, so people who navigate by headings will not find it.

<h2 id="usage">Usage policy and cognitive accessibility</h2>

Start each section with a heading that says what the cards below do, such as “Kitchen lights” rather than “Lights 1”. Use the title style for a section and the subtitle style for a group inside it. Keep one subject per heading. If a heading acts as a link, say where it goes in its text. See [Dashboard composition and card features](../home-assistant/dashboard-composition.html).

Success criteria that apply:

- 1.3.1 Info and Relationships: the section row is not a heading.
- 2.4.6 Headings and Labels and 2.4.10 Section Headings: each section has a heading that describes it.
- 1.4.3 Contrast (Minimum): check the section row label colour on your own dashboard.

